{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310629,"nonce":"j0ACIJvWC77O0iX3QAGVUuKJqaM=","title":"D12 FIXED 2026-09-05 (L1 a-d + L3, see status block). Root: `haxe.Constraints.IMap` is never loaded because the module-subtype resolver ...","message":"**Landed:** commits 72b574b4 (devirt env) af61b4fb (map slot adapters) edd52081 (KeyValueIterator protocol) a7c1041c (erased Null\u003cT\u003e boundaries) 721e10d0 (typer IMap identity); battery 439/439 vs conf_d9c, GAINED Issue3635 / LOST Issue12700 both bistable on one binary (12700: 2/5 PASS).\n\nThe chain the workflow predicted held, with one correction: L1(c)'s kind fix-up was inert because\nthe receiver bound to a THIRD symbol — a typeless Class placeholder minted by\n`import haxe.Constraints.IMap` in haxe/ds/Map.hx (imports.rs qualified-name-mismatch branch),\nnot to the typedef symbol. Fixes: import placeholders take the declared kind (scan the source for\n`interface X`) and always carry a type (a typeless one left IntMap's `this` untyped ⇒ no wrap);\na colliding interface registers under its package only (`haxe.IMap`) and lowering looks the\npackaged symbol up first; `pkg.Module.Name` retries with the module segment dropped (imports +\ndotted annotations); interface METHODS take the interface scope so they get qualified names\n(`haxe.IMap.get`) — without that every member was synthesized typeless and `im.keys()` had no\nprotocol type ⇒ the for-in emitted NO LOOP (silent drop). Root-package types have no qualified\nname ⇒ method lookup falls back to the bare name. Companion fixes:\n[[bugs-devirtualizer-dropped-closure-env]], [[bugs-erased-null-t-box-at-type-param-boundary]],\nKeyValueIterator recognised as an iterator protocol (element = the pair).\nTRAP: `RAYZOR_IGNORE_EMBEDDED_SNAPSHOT=1` changed nothing — the snapshot was NOT the culprit.\n\n**Symptom:** `m.keyValueIterator()` on StringMap/IntMap traps \"`IMap.keys` was never\ncompiled\" (harness g4a/g4b, exit 134/132). `var m:IMap\u003cString,Int\u003e = ...; m.bogus()`\nCOMPILES and traps — rayzor accepts invalid Haxe here.\n\n\n**L1 — IMap never exists as an Interface** (four stacked front-end facts):\n(a) `compiler/src/tast/namespace.rs:310-318` sub-type resolver matched only the\nliterals `interface IMap ` / `class X{`; `haxe/Constraints.hx:67` reads\n`interface IMap\u003cK, V\u003e {`, so `haxe.Constraints.IMap` (the ONLY spelling anyone\nuses) is unresolvable and `compilation.rs:3683` `continue`s: Constraints.hx is in\nNO import order, ever. Refuter twin: `import Cons.IGen;` with `interface IGen\u003cT\u003e`\nfails identically; `interface INon {` works. FIXED 5c42a916: match keyword+name followed by any\nnon-identifier char. Constraints.hx now in every import order; `import Cons.IGen`\n(generic sub-type) works; g4a now traps on the SLOT thunk\n`__vtable_dispatch_thunk__haxe_ds_StringMap_keys` = layer L3 reached; g4b SIGSEGV.\nBattery 436 -\u003e 435 = Issue12700 FLAKE only (3/5 PASS on the same binary,\n`1 != 0.000…`, a float/int nondeterminism recorded since the compile-order work).\n(b) root `haxe-std/Map.hx:26` `typedef IMap\u003cK,V\u003e = haxe.Constraints.IMap\u003cK,V\u003e` is\npre-registered as a bare SymbolKind::Class `IMap` (registration.rs:487-512\n\"Reuse class for typedefs\"); `types/mod.rs:126-141` dotted-name fallback ACCEPTS a\nsymbol with no qualified_name for `haxe.Constraints.IMap\u003cK,V\u003e` (\"extern classes\nmay not have qualified names set\") -\u003e TypeKind::Class{IMap,[K,V]}.\n(c) registration.rs:277-287 Interface branch early-returns on a root-name\ncollision with NO kind fix-up (the Enum branch :318-335 HAS one);\n`lower_interface_declaration` reuses the Class symbol. **TRIED 2026-09-05 and\nREVERTED: mirroring the Enum fix-up (kind/type/qualified name) changed NOTHING for\nthe field-typed (`imap_l2b`) and return-typed (`imap_l2c`) shapes — both still trap\non the synthesized `haxe.Constraints.IMap.exists` — and the battery was flat\n(435; Issue3635's one CRASH was a load flake: 5/5 PASS on the same binary). The\nmember is synthesized BEFORE the kind is fixed, or via a different symbol: (b)/(d)\nare the next lever (probe: which symbol `haxe.Constraints.IMap\u003cString,Int\u003e` binds\nto in Holder's field type — types/mod.rs:126-141 fallback).** Note `var im:IMap =\nnew StringMap()` (imap_l2a/ctl) MATCHES because the receiver narrows to StringMap\nand the runtime mapping is called directly — accidental, not dispatch.\n(d) On a Class-kinded receiver, unresolved members get SYNTHESIZED Function\nplaceholders `\u003cclass\u003e.\u003cmethod\u003e` (calls.rs:418-430) -\u003e `try_forward_declared_call`\n(forward_ref.rs) emits a direct call to a bodyless stub -\u003e LLVM trap by name.\nOrder-dependent: once a module has synthesized `IMap.get`, later modules' `im.get`\nbind to that stub via external_function_name_map; `im.set` (never synthesized)\nfalls through to the runtime mapping and WORKS by accident.\n\n**L2 — coercion wraps:** `maybe_wrap_for_interface` already runs at var-init,\nctor-arg and return; `register_class_metadata` will insert (StringMap, IMap) once\n`implements[i]` is TypeKind::Interface. No new code expected.\n\n**L3 — extern-map slots:** StringMap/IntMap/ObjectMap methods are RUNTIME MAPPING\nrows (runtime_mapping.rs:2848-2949), never MIR functions, so a fat-pointer slot can\nonly get an empty by-name stub. Needs adapter thunks `(env, this, erased args) -\u003e\nerased return` per method: keys/iterator -\u003e the mir_wrapper (returns ArrayIterator,\nmust become an ITER HANDLE for the consumer); get -\u003e raw u64 must be BOXED as the\nconcrete V known at the coercion site (D10 shape); set: raw_value_params mask;\nexists/remove -\u003e Bool; toString -\u003e String; clear; copy has NO runtime function.\nDesign sketch lives in the workflow journal\n(`subagents/workflows/wf_5f8fd66e-8fa/journal.jsonl`, probe:adapter-design).\n\n**Downstream defects found by the refuters (NOT IMap-specific):**\n- A same-file mirror of g4a with a REAL interface and compiled methods still gives\n  the wrong loop count; `RAYZOR_NO_SRA=1` fixes it -\u003e the scalar-replacement pass\n  (`compiler/src/ir/scalar_replacement.rs`) drops field stores of an INLINED\n  constructor. Separate optimizer bug; repro under `scratchpad/wf2_refute/`.\n- A value returned by an interface-dispatched `keys():Iterator\u003cK\u003e` is a raw\n  iterator, not an ITER HANDLE, so a consumer typed `Iterator\u003cK\u003e` reads it as\n  exhausted or crashes — the same boundary rule as\n  `wrap_stdlib_iter_result` (D4) must apply to interface-slot returns.\n- L4 (`haxe.ds.Map` abstract on an unresolved multiType, Issue6457/6833): THE\n  ABSTRACT CALLS ITSELF (`fn @haxe.ds.Map.keys` -\u003e its own `keys`), not IMap\n  dispatch; unresolved `new Map()` picks the abstract's own body. Separate (D11).\n\n**Method:** `rayzor run Main.hx` WITHOUT a rayzor.toml adds NO class path\n(src/main.rs:3828-3847), so sibling files are never read — every multi-file probe\nneeds `rayzor.toml` with `class-paths=[\".\"]` or it is confounded (E0200).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_imap_never_loads_generic_subtype_import` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}